# MineQTT Docker host table: the remote Docker hosts that docker/client-test/run.sh, docker/client-test/remote-gc.sh and
# e2e/lanes/lane.sh may use, in the order --host auto tries them (this workstation comes after all of them).
#
# The real table is not tracked. docker/hosts.sh reads the first of these files that exists:
#   1. $MINEQTT_HOSTS_FILE
#   2. <git common dir>/mineqtt-docker-hosts, e.g. .git/mineqtt-docker-hosts (shared by every worktree of the clone)
#   3. docker/hosts.local (ignored by git)
# Copy this file to one of them and replace the rows. Without a table there are no remotes and auto runs locally.
#
# One host per line, columns separated by blanks; lines starting with # and blank lines are skipped.
#   name      short name: the --host value, the suffix of its client slot dir, the name in messages. Per-host
#             overrides use it upper-cased with - as _: MINEQTT_SLOTS_BUILD_HOST, MINEQTT_LANES_BUILD_HOST
#   endpoint  ssh://user@host (docker -H; docker.exe on Windows uses Windows OpenSSH, so the key and the known_hosts
#             entry must be in %USERPROFILE%\.ssh), or the name of a Docker context
#   slots     client test stacks at once (run.sh)
#   cpus mem  size of one client stack (run.sh; CLIENT_CPUS / CLIENT_MEMORY override it)
#   lanes     lanes at once (lane.sh, checked by auto)
#   cpuset    CPUs every MineQTT container is pinned to (docker --cpuset-cpus, e.g. 4-7,12-15), or - for none
#   shares    docker --cpu-shares of every MineQTT container (256: a quarter of Docker's default weight, so the
#             host's own services win every CPU contention), or - for Docker's default weight. cpuset and shares are
#             set together or not at all
#   build     auto: images are built and the Gradle seed filled whenever a run needs them; manual: only on an
#             explicit --host (lane.sh build, run.sh --warm), and auto skips the host until they exist
#
# The first row is a dedicated build host. The second is a shared machine that runs other services (production, for
# example) and is used only as throttled overflow: few slots, MineQTT containers pinned to whole cores of its own
# (lscpu -e shows which CPUs share a core) and weighted down with cpu shares, and build=manual, because image builds,
# pulls and the Gradle warm-up cannot be pinned and so happen there only on request, at a quiet hour.
#
# name      endpoint                        slots cpus mem lanes cpuset     shares build
build-host  ssh://user@build-host.example   16    3    5g  20    -          -      auto
overflow    ssh://user@overflow.example      2    3    5g   6    4-7,12-15  256    manual
